{{!
    @template local_moodesk/kb_article

    Knowledge base — one article.

    The breadcrumb says where the article sits; the header is its identity and,
    for editors, its actions (built by kb_article_view, never here). Below, one
    reading surface labelled by the page's own <h1>: a meta line saying where the
    article is filed, who it is for and when it last moved — plus who moved it,
    for editors — then the body inside `.mhd-prose`, then the way to a ticket.

    Who is looking is decided in \local_moodesk\output\kb_article_view, once:
    this template renders what it is given and asks no capability question.

    `renderedbody` has been through format_text() — that is what the name
    promises, and tests/kb_html_rendering_test.php holds every template to it.

    Transitions are one POST each — action, sesskey — and split by what they
    are. The workflow's next step (Publish on a draft, Restore on an archived
    article) is the header's primary action; its form is hidden here and the
    header's button submits it by id through the HTML `form` attribute. The
    administrative ones (Unpublish, Archive, Delete) are a footer inside the
    article, outlined, after the text. A form is rendered only when the
    article's status and the user's capability allow that transition; there is
    no disabled state to explain.

    Context variables:
      * breadcrumb     - breadcrumb partial context (Knowledge base › Category › title)
      * pageheader     - page_header context (title; status meta and actions for editors)
      * renderedbody   - The body, rendered by format_text()
      * haspluginsections / pluginsections[] - {html} sections plugins add (hook kb_article_view_extend)
      * plugintop[]    - {html} sections above the article (same hook)
      * pluginfacts[]  - {label, html} facts in the meta line (same hook)
      * hasbody        - False when the article has no text yet
      * isdraft        - True for a draft (the empty-body hint says how to publish)
      * iseditor       - Whether the viewer gets the editorial layers
      * categoryname   - The category's name, or "General"
      * categoryurl    - The landing filtered on that category
      * audiencelabel  - "Everyone" / "Agents only"
      * agentsonly     - True when the audience is agents
      * timemodified   - Last edit, formatted
      * haseditor      - True when the last editor is known (editors only)
      * editorname     - Who last edited it (editors only)
      * haspublished   - True when the article has ever been published (editors only)
      * timepublished  - First publication, formatted (editors only)
      * cta            - {show, url, text, button}: "Open a ticket"
      * actionurl      - This page, the target of every transition form
      * sesskey        - The session key
      * canpublish, canunpublish, canarchive, canrestore, candelete
                       - Which transition forms to render
      * haslifecycle   - True when any of unpublish / archive / delete renders
      * htmllang       - `lang` for the article surface when the row is not in the page's language, else ""

    Example context (json):
    {
      "pageheader": {
        "title": "How to reset your password",
        "description": null,
        "meta": "<span class=\"mhd-pill mhd-pill--success\">Published</span>",
        "actions": [],
        "primaryaction": {
          "label": "Edit", "url": "/local/moodesk/kb_article_edit.php?id=7", "hasurl": true, "hasform": false,
          "icon": "edit", "hasicon": true, "icononly": false, "variant": "filled", "attributes": [], "hasattributes": false
        },
        "hasactions": true
      },
      "breadcrumb": {"label": "Breadcrumb", "items": [
        {"label": "Knowledge base", "url": "/local/moodesk/kb.php", "current": false},
        {"label": "Access", "url": "/local/moodesk/kb.php?category=3", "current": false},
        {"label": "How to reset your password", "url": null, "current": true}
      ]},
      "renderedbody": "<p>Click <strong>Forgot password</strong> on the login page.</p>",
      "hasbody": true,
      "isdraft": false,
      "iseditor": true,
      "categoryname": "Access",
      "categoryurl": "/local/moodesk/kb.php?category=3",
      "audiencelabel": "Everyone",
      "agentsonly": false,
      "timemodified": "12 Sep 2026, 10:42",
      "haseditor": true,
      "editorname": "Alba Agente",
      "haspublished": true,
      "timepublished": "10 Sep 2026, 09:00",
      "cta": {"show": true, "url": "/local/moodesk/submit.php?categoryid=3", "text": "Didn't find what you needed?", "button": "Open a ticket"},
      "actionurl": "/local/moodesk/kb_article.php?id=7",
      "sesskey": "abc123",
      "canpublish": false,
      "canunpublish": true,
      "canarchive": true,
      "canrestore": false,
      "candelete": true,
      "haslifecycle": true,
      "htmllang": ""
    }
}}
<div class="mhd-kb-article">

  {{#breadcrumb}}{{> local_moodesk/breadcrumb }}{{/breadcrumb}}

  {{#pageheader}}{{> local_moodesk/page_header }}{{/pageheader}}

  {{! Labelled by the page's own <h1> (page_header renders it with a fixed id),
      so the article has a heading without the title being drawn twice. }}
  {{! Plugin sections under the header (hook kb_article_view_extend). }}
  {{#plugintop}}{{{html}}}{{/plugintop}}

  <article class="mhd-kb-article__surface" aria-labelledby="mhd-page-title"{{#htmllang}} lang="{{htmllang}}"{{/htmllang}}>

    {{! The facts about the article that are not its text. A reader gets where
        it is filed, who it is for and when it changed; an editor also gets who
        changed it and when it first went live. Absent, not blank. }}
    <dl class="mhd-kb-article__meta">
      <div class="mhd-kb-article__fact">
        <dt>{{#str}} kb_col_category, local_moodesk {{/str}}</dt>
        <dd><a href="{{categoryurl}}" class="mhd-kb-article__category">{{categoryname}}</a></dd>
      </div>
      {{#agentsonly}}
      <div class="mhd-kb-article__fact">
        <dt>{{#str}} kb_field_audience, local_moodesk {{/str}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--outline">{{audiencelabel}}</span></dd>
      </div>
      {{/agentsonly}}
      <div class="mhd-kb-article__fact">
        <dt>{{#str}} kb_col_updated, local_moodesk {{/str}}</dt>
        <dd>{{timemodified}}{{#haseditor}} <span class="mhd-kb-article__by">{{#str}} kb_updated_by, local_moodesk, {{editorname}} {{/str}}</span>{{/haseditor}}</dd>
      </div>
      {{#haspublished}}
      <div class="mhd-kb-article__fact">
        <dt>{{#str}} kb_first_published, local_moodesk {{/str}}</dt>
        <dd>{{timepublished}}</dd>
      </div>
      {{/haspublished}}
      {{#pluginfacts}}
      <div class="mhd-kb-article__fact">
        <dt>{{label}}</dt>
        <dd>{{{html}}}</dd>
      </div>
      {{/pluginfacts}}
    </dl>

    {{#hasbody}}
    <div class="mhd-prose">{{{renderedbody}}}</div>
    {{/hasbody}}
    {{^hasbody}}
    <p class="mhd-kb-article__empty text-muted">
      {{#str}} kb_body_empty, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      {{#isdraft}}{{#iseditor}}{{#str}} kb_body_empty_hint, local_moodesk {{/str}}{{/iseditor}}{{/isdraft}}
    </p>
    {{/hasbody}}

    {{! "Was this article helpful?" (KB-07) — after the text, before the
        way out, so the reader answers about what they just read. Absent,
        not disabled, when there is nothing to ask. }}

    {{! Sections plugins add (hook kb_article_view_extend). }}
    {{#haspluginsections}}
    {{#pluginsections}}{{{html}}}{{/pluginsections}}
    {{/haspluginsections}}

    {{! The way out when the answer was not here — filed under this article's
        category when it is still one a ticket can be opened in. }}
    {{#cta}}{{#show}}
    <aside class="mhd-kb-article__cta">
      <p class="mhd-kb-article__cta-text">{{text}}</p>
      <a href="{{url}}" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined">{{button}}</a>
    </aside>
    {{/show}}{{/cta}}

    {{! The administrative transitions — the ones that take an article off the
        shelf or away for good. At the foot of the article rather than in the
        header, and outlined: they are deliberate, occasional acts a manager
        takes after reading, and nothing about them should out-rank Edit or
        the workflow's next step, which is what the header holds. Rendered
        only for a holder of :managekb — absent, not disabled, for anyone
        else. Delete asks first, with the browser's own confirm, the same way
        Webhooks and Automations do. }}
    {{#haslifecycle}}
    <footer class="mhd-kb-article__lifecycle">
      <span class="mhd-kb-article__lifecycle-label">{{#str}} kb_lifecycle_heading, local_moodesk {{/str}}</span>
      <div class="mhd-action-group">
        {{#canunpublish}}
        <form method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
          <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="unpublish">
          <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
          <button type="submit" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--small">{{#str}} kb_action_unpublish, local_moodesk {{/str}}</button>
        </form>
        {{/canunpublish}}
        {{#canarchive}}
        <form method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
          <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="archive">
          <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
          <button type="submit" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--small">
            <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#mhd-icon-archive"></use></svg>
            {{#str}} kb_action_archive, local_moodesk {{/str}}
          </button>
        </form>
        {{/canarchive}}
        {{#candelete}}
        <form method="post" action="{{actionurl}}"
              onsubmit="return confirm('{{#str}} kb_delete_confirm, local_moodesk {{/str}}');">
          <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="delete">
          <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
          <button type="submit" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined-danger mhd-btn--small">
            <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#mhd-icon-trash"></use></svg>
            {{#str}} kb_action_delete, local_moodesk {{/str}}
          </button>
        </form>
        {{/candelete}}
      </div>
    </footer>
    {{/haslifecycle}}

  </article>

  {{! The workflow's next step lives in the header as its primary action, and
      the header only holds the button: the request it submits is spelled out
      here, one hidden form with an id the button points at through the HTML
      `form` attribute. Rendered only when the article's status and the user's
      capability allow that transition. }}
  {{#canpublish}}
  <form id="mhd-kb-action-publish" method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="publish">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
  </form>
  {{/canpublish}}
  {{#canrestore}}
  <form id="mhd-kb-action-restore" method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="restore">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
  </form>
  {{/canrestore}}

</div>
